NAME
        nodetool placement - Inspect data placement and replica relationships

SYNOPSIS
        nodetool [(-h <host> | --host <host>)] [(-p <port> | --port <port>)]
                [(-pw <password> | --password <password>)]
                [(-pwf <passwordFilePath> | --password-file <passwordFilePath>)]
                [(-u <username> | --username <username>)] placement <command> [<args>]

        nodetool [(-h <host> | --host <host>)] [(-p <port> | --port <port>)]
                [(-pw <password> | --password <password>)]
                [(-pwf <passwordFilePath> | --password-file <passwordFilePath>)]
                [(-u <username> | --username <username>)] placement peers [--catch-up]
                [(-dc <specific_dc> | --in-dc <specific_dc>)...]
                [(-f <format> | --format <format>)]
                [(-k <keyspace> | --keyspaces <keyspace>)...]
                [(-n <node> | --node <node>)]
                [(-x <exclude_keyspace> | --exclude-keyspaces <exclude_keyspace>)...]

OPTIONS
        -h <host>, --host <host>
            Node hostname or ip address

        -p <port>, --port <port>
            Remote jmx agent port number

        -pw <password>, --password <password>
            Remote jmx agent password

        -pwf <passwordFilePath>, --password-file <passwordFilePath>
            Path to the JMX password file

        -u <username>, --username <username>
            Remote jmx agent username

COMMANDS
        With no arguments, Display help information

        peers
            Display replica peers for a node. Replica peers are nodes that share
            ownership of the same token ranges. This information helps avoid performing
            concurrent operations on a node and its peers.

            With --node option, The node to display peers for (accepts Node ID, Host
            ID, or IP address). Includes all nodes when this option is not specified.
            (Mutually exclusive with --in-dc)

            With --in-dc option, Limits the report to nodes that belong to the
            specified datacenters. This option can be repeated to include multiple
            datacenters. Includes all datacenters when it is not specified. (Mutually
            exclusive with --node)

            With --keyspaces option, Include only these keyspaces (comma-separated).
            Includes all keyspaces when this option is not specified. Providing a
            single keyspace shows peers based on its specific replication factor.

            With --exclude-keyspaces option, Exclude these keyspaces (comma-separated)
            from the report.

            With --catch-up option, Fetch the latest metadata from the CMS before
            executing. Fails if synchronization is not possible.

            With --format option, Output format: yaml, json, minified-yaml, or
            minified-json. Case-insensitive. (Default: yaml)
